title: "FAIL — A Computational Audit of Randomized Two-Bin Stretching"
message: "If you use this negative-result audit or its reproduction script, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Yonezu
    given-names: Ryutaro
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-09
repository-code: "https://github.com/yonezaemon1-hub/randomized-bin-stretching-failed-transfer-audit"
abstract: >-
  Negative-result and soundness-audit package for a failed transfer in randomized online two-bin stretching. The package exactly reproduces the classic 7/6 Yao support and gives an exact offline-feasible diagnostic showing that a naive joint-state pruning/lifting rule does not certify the apparent 57/46 candidate. No new competitive-ratio bound is claimed.
keywords:
  - online bin stretching
  - randomized algorithms
  - negative result
  - soundness audit
  - exact arithmetic
  - reproducibility
